n work for many hair types, but buyers with very thick, coarse, or tightly curly hair may want a more powerful or specialized straightening tool.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>How do I reduce frizz when straightening?</summary><p class="faq-answer">Start with dry hair, use reasonable section sizes, apply heat protectant, avoid excessive heat, and choose a tool with smooth plates and stable temperature control.</p></details>
